<span class="eyebrow">Data Transparency</span>
<h1>Agricultural Data Sources & Updates</h1>
<p class="lede">GoOrganicAfrica is designed to keep time-sensitive farming data current while clearly separating official statistics from our farming assumptions and market estimates.</p>
<h2>What can change automatically?</h2>
<ul>
<li>Commodity market/reference prices</li><li><strong>Seed prices</strong> and planting-material costs when a reliable machine-readable source is available</li><li>Fertilizer and other input prices when a reliable source is configured</li><li>Currency exchange rates where a trusted feed is configured</li><li>Government statistics and publication dates</li>
</ul>
<h2>Why review is required</h2>
<p>A new government publication can contain several tables, units and regional averages. GoOrganicAfrica therefore records the source and proposes changes for review instead of blindly guessing a value. Approved changes are committed to the website repository and automatically trigger a new site deployment.</p>
<h2>Seed prices</h2>
<p>Seed prices are treated as a separate data class because the price of a named variety, hybrid, brand and pack size can change independently of the commodity's selling price. Where no reliable public feed exists, the CMS provides the manual override until a suitable source is configured.</p>
<h2>Important disclaimer</h2>
<p>Calculator outputs are estimates, not guarantees. Actual prices and costs vary by location, variety, supplier, season, farm size and market conditions. Always confirm local prices before making a major investment.</p>
</div></section>
